 "note": "APPEND-ONLY successor (Codex serving review round 13, owner-approved). CODE EXECUTION REMOVED: the bundled scorer.py path (arbitrary code execution reproduced by Codex) is gone \u2014 the scorer is BAKED into the loader image as medzen_model_loader/scorer_v1.py, resolved by predeclared scorer_id + the sha256 of the baked module's own bytes (platform/promotion/scorer_v1.py is the byte-pinned reference copy); a bundle carrying ANY executable file refuses before the gate runs; nothing from evidence is compiled. SIGNING AUTHORITY INDEPENDENT: infra/promotion_admission.tf creates the DEDICATED medzen-promotion-admission-role (OIDC trust = the promotion-admission environment + model-pipeline.yml@master, the arm-launch pattern) and REPLACES the signing key's policy: the account root administers but CANNOT sign; kms:Sign (ECDSA_SHA_256, DIGEST only) is granted to the admission role and nothing else \u2014 applied LIVE and proven with a real denied kms:Sign as the local admin user and implicit denies for trainer/arm-launch/asr roles; the RSASSA_PSS template trap is corrected to ECDSA. ROWS BOUND TO THE JOB: the gate report's sealed_outputs name versioned S3 objects under the sealed job's OWN output prefix; admission fetches each by VersionId, requires the bytes to hash to the declaration, the write time inside the job's [CreationTime, EndTime] window, the bundled row bytes to EQUAL the object, and the job's own INFERENCE RECEIPT (also an output object) to attest this artifact tree, the predeclared decoding_config_sha256, the contract image, the job name and every row sha; the runtime verifies the signed attestation offline against the bundled rows. CONTRACT COMPLETE: environment_sha256, full channel semantics (data type, distribution, content type, compression, input mode), VPC config, max runtime, instance count, volume size, checkpoint config and the output artifact identity are predeclared, live-described and exactly compared; image references must be well-formed immutable ECR digests (repo@sha256:x refuses); network isolation is REQUIRED; licence and reservation documents are opened, hashed against the registry and must name the set's manifest. ONE DETERMINISTIC ADMISSION PATH: scripts/assemble_promotion_bundle.py runs the complete live gate, lays out the bundle, signs the authority and the evidence ROOT (bundle.json) with KMS, then runs the loader's OWN verifier and DELETES any bundle the runtime refuses; model-pipeline.yml runs it in the protected environment under the admission role and opens an append-only admission-record PR (no placeholder exit, no shell interpolation). REHEARSED end to end against immutable synthetic evidence in tests/test_b6v2_assembler_rehearsal.py. CI IMAGES: model-images.yml builds, Trivy-scans (fail-closed) and SBOMs the exact loader and GPU Dockerfiles; push-by-digest with provenance mode=max is gated on the CI role. ARM-1: receipt -002 (VersionIds, KMS identity, UTC corrected, 20 periodic + 2 rolling + 1 export); frozen dev selection (420 rows, 10 pools byte-verified against their committed sha256s); hardened sweep executor (version-bound reads, digest-pinned images, create-only uploads) running development-only \u2014 no sealed set read. OPEN (owner): create the GitHub promotion-admission environment with required review and set MEDZEN_ADMISSION_ROLE_ARN; until then the admission role's trust matches no token (fail-closed).",
